The paper is above the medium-scoring anchors that were rejected (SPARK at 5.25, ArticulateRules at 5.0) because it has a cleaner conceptual framework, recovers known findings (indirect validation), and discovers genuinely new patterns. But it is below the accepted medium anchors (Scylla at 6.25) because the counterfactual validation concern is more central to the method's core claims. The paper sits in the borderline range.

