The Definition 4 inconsistency reveals a deeper tension in the paper: the earliest-disagreement concept is fundamentally about the *interaction* between two treatment processes (observed and counterfactual), yet the formal definition treats only one as first-class. This suggests the augmented process construction, while elegant for ensuring P_obs marginal consistency, may not be the right abstraction for capturing the symmetric nature of the disagreement. A formulation where δ is defined symmetrically over both treatment processes — with the augmented process constructed to maintain consistency at the (single) event time t+δ — might yield a cleaner theoretical foundation.

