2. **Parameter-free methods (NGM and PS-GM) achieve O(L₀R²/ε + [L₁R]²) without knowing (L₀, L₁)**: Theorems 4.1 and 5.1 show that both NGM and PS-GM match the (pessimistic) convex GM rate while automatically adapting to the best possible (L₀, L₁) pair (as noted at the end of Section 4 and Section 5). This improves over Takezawa et al. (2024), who require additional L-smoothness and obtain O(L₀R²/ε + √(L/ε)L₁R²).

